#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:138
msgid ""
"This class provides a unified interface for compiling and executing TileLang "
"kernels. It supports two execution modes that are automatically inferred:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:142
msgid "Execution Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:143
msgid ""
"**lazy**: The decorated function returns a PrimFunc explicitly. Calling the "
"JIT wrapper returns a compiled kernel object, which can be invoked "
"separately. This mode is useful when you want to inspect or reuse the kernel "
"object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:147
msgid "Example (lazy mode)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:149
msgid ""
"@tilelang.jit(out_idx=[-1])\n"
"def matmul(M, N, K, block_M, block_N, block_K):\n"
"    @T.prim_func\n"
"    def kernel(A: T.Tensor((M, K), dtype), ...):\n"
"        ...\n"
"    return kernel  # explicitly return PrimFunc\n"
"\n"
"kernel = matmul(1024, 1024, 1024, 128, 128, 32)  # returns kernel\n"
"result = kernel(a, b)  # execute separately"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:159
msgid ""
"**eager**: The decorated function uses the DSL builder pattern with tensor "
"type annotations. Calling the JIT wrapper compiles and immediately executes "
"the kernel, returning the result directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:163
msgid "Example (eager mode)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:165
msgid ""
"@tilelang.jit\n"
"def gemm(A, B, C, block_M: int = 64):\n"
"    M, N, K = T.const(\"M N K\")\n"
"    A: T.Tensor[[M, K], dtype]  # tensor shape via annotation\n"
"    B: T.Tensor[[K, N], dtype]\n"
"    C: T.Tensor[[M, N], dtype]\n"
"    with T.Kernel(...):\n"
"        ...\n"
"\n"
"gemm(A, B, C)  # compiles and executes immediately"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/jit/index.rst:176
msgid ""
"The mode is automatically inferred based on whether the function returns a "
"PrimFunc (lazy) or uses the builder pattern (eager)."
msgstr ""

